      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We assessed each tool against a realistic fan-trip scenario: a fixed event on a fixed date in an unfamiliar city, with flights, accommodation, tickets, and matchday logistics to coordinate. Evaluation drew on vendor documentation, published feature sets, and community consensus from traveling supporters, following the <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a>.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Event awareness (30%)</strong> — does the tool know the event exists, when it is, and where, or does it treat the trip like any other city break?</li>
        <li><strong>Trip coherence (25%)</strong> — flights, stays, tickets, and budget pulled into one plan instead of five tabs</li>
        <li><strong>Cost visibility (20%)</strong> — full-trip budget estimates including tickets, the cost fans most often underestimate</li>
        <li><strong>City &amp; venue context (15%)</strong> — neighborhood guidance, stadium information, and matchday logistics</li>
        <li><strong>Cost &amp; friction (10%)</strong> — price to use and how much manual coordination remains</li>
      </ul>

